# $CUSTOM_BASH_DIR/.bash_profile_plain is sourced once at shell startup
# (before abp is called). Use it for env vars or bootstrapping that must
# be available immediately, without running abp first.
#
# Most things belong in .bash_profile_before (env vars for abp) or
# .bash_profile_after (tool loading after abp). Only put things here
# that are genuinely needed at login time before abp.
#
# Example — uncomment to activate rvm:
# source "$HOME/.rvm/scripts/rvm"
